    "result_text": "All 260 tests pass, build succeeds. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule in the Spring PetClinic REST app.\n\n**The rule:** when more than 80 owners have already been created on a given day, the owner response includes `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (read-only) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Marked `bulkSignupWarning` as `@Mapping(ignore = true)` on `toOwnerDto`, since it isn't derivable from the `Owner` entity alone (it depends on a global per-day count) and is set by the controller.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added a `ownersCreatedOn(LocalDate)` helper that counts owners by their business-day registration date \u2014 reusing the exact accumulation path as the existing daily create-limit rule.\n   - In `addOwner`, set `bulkSignupWarning = ownersCreatedThatDay > 80` (the pre-save count of owners already created that day \u2014 i.e. \"more than 80 already created\").\n   - In `getOwner`, set it from `ownersCreatedOn(owner.getRegistrationDate()) > 80`, so a retrieved owner reports the same warning consistently.\n\n**Design notes:**\n- I used `> 80` (strictly more than 80), matching the spec's \"more than 80... already been created.\"\n- The count keys on the business-day registration date, consistent with the existing per-day cap rule (`>= 100` \u2192 429), which the acceptance test comment explicitly ties to (\"shares the same accumulation path\").\n\nThe full suite passes: **260 tests, 0 failures**, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` which asserts `bulkSignupWarning` is `false` for a fresh create.",
